From d1034a3ea6e37ad0ab165891b7f6c29df608f4b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:06:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] SableOS: battery health and usage model with host tests

Pure Java (no android.* imports) model for the SableOS Battery
design (BATTERY_HEALTH_USAGE_UX, BH1-BH5):

* HealthFact with availability, source, confidence and sample time;
  BatteryHealthEvaluator fails closed: strict facts (capacity, cycle
  count, charge counter, dates) need device-profile evidence, values
  are sanity-checked, nothing is estimated.
* CapacityMath, HealthFactPresenter (month-precision dates, coarse
  age), TemperatureClass.
* BatteryCapabilityProfile + BatteryProfileParser: the per-device
  capability schema, loaded from data, every key UNKNOWN by default.
* ChargingControlPolicy: BH5 discovery states; BH6 mutation is a
  compile-time false, so no control can become interactive.
* HistoryRingBuffer/HistoryBuckets/HistoryRange: bounded local
  history (7 days, at most one sample per 30 minutes).
* ChartInspectionCursor, SegmentedRangeGroup, TypeAheadMatcher,
  ListFocusNavigator: keyboard contracts as state machines.
* UsageSummary: top consumers over one accounting window.

SettingsSableBatteryModelTests runs them on the host JVM.
